# 5. ABSTRACT
h_abs = doc.add_paragraph()
h_abs.alignment = WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER
r = h_abs.add_run("ABSTRACT")
r.font.bold = True
r.font.size = Pt(16)
r.font.color.rgb = RGBColor(0, 51, 102)

add_p(
    "In the modern digital retail landscape, e-commerce platforms feature"
    " complex, dynamic pricing structures where catalog prices and customer"
    " ratings fluctuate continuously. Manual tracking and comparison of book"
    " prices across multi-page web catalogs is inefficient, highly error-prone,"
    " and analytically infeasible. This Cornerstone Project implements an"
    " automated, end-to-end Web Scraping and Product Price Analysis System"
    " built entirely in Python."
)
add_p(
    "The data ingestion pipeline utilizes the Requests library and"
    " BeautifulSoup4 to systematically crawl 12 pagination pages of an"
    " e-commerce book catalog (books.toscrape.com), extracting 240 product"
    " records without server connection drops. Extracted raw features include"
    " product title, raw text price (with currency formatting), CSS-based"
    " rating classes, and stock availability strings. The pipeline executes"
    " robust data cleaning protocols: currency stripping, numeric float64"
    " casting, dictionary-based ordinal rating transformation (converting text"
    " words 'One' through 'Five' into numeric integers 1 to 5), regex-driven"
    " stock parsing, duplicate detection, and missing-value imputation"
    " verification."
)
add_p(
    "Feature engineering is performed to enrich the dataset with analytical"
    " dimensions: categorical economic price binning (Low, Mid, High tiers),"
    " baseline Maximum Retail Price (MRP) calculation at 1.25x markup, and"
    " derived discount percentages. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) and visual"
    " analytics are implemented using Matplotlib and Seaborn, producing an"
    " integrated 4-panel dashboard containing price distribution histograms"
    " with Kernel Density Estimation (KDE), bar graphs of average price by"
    " rating tier, average price trend lines, and price-tier inventory counts."
    " The experimental results reveal that product ratings and prices are"
    " distributed independently across this catalog, demonstrating that premium"
    " ratings do not carry an exorbitant price markup. The system successfully"
    " exports an analysis-ready tabular dataset (cleaned_books_data.csv),"
    " delivering a robust model for automated retail intelligence."
)

