    "The exponential growth of the World Wide Web and digital commercial"
    " ecosystems has radically transformed modern commerce. Today, millions of"
    " retail transactions take place across dynamic online platforms. Retail"
    " pricing structures are sensitive to supply chain fluctuations, inventory"
    " volumes, and algorithmic demand shifts. For consumers seeking optimal"
    " purchasing decisions and data analysts evaluating market dynamics,"
    " manual inspection of e-commerce websites is infeasible. Web scraping has"
    " emerged as a vital methodology for extracting unstructured web content"
    " into structured, machine-readable datasets."
)
add_p(
    "Web scraping programmatically queries HTTP endpoints, retrieves HTML"
    " document trees, and parses DOM nodes to capture target data points such"
    " as product titles, current prices, stock metrics, and ratings. This"
    " project, entitled “Web Scraping and Product Price Analysis System,”"
    " develops a robust, automated Python pipeline to collect, clean,"
    " transform, and analyze product data from an e-commerce platform"
    " (books.toscrape.com). By combining Requests, BeautifulSoup, Pandas, and"
    " Seaborn, the system delivers an end-to-end retail intelligence framework."
)
for p in expand_text(
    "automated web crawling and data science pipeline architecture", 3
):
